<title>GREECE: GREEK BOURSE SUPERVISOR ORDERS AUDIT OF 10 BROKERS.</title>
<headline>GREEK BOURSE SUPERVISOR ORDERS AUDIT OF 10 BROKERS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Athens bourse supervisor George Malakis ordered inspectors to audit seven brokerage firms on Tuesday, according to a circular sent to national economy ministry general secretary Apostolos Fotiadis.</p>
<p>The seven brokerage firms are the following:</p>
<p>Euroxx Securities</p>
<p>N.D.Devletoglou Securities</p>
<p>Beta Securities</p>
<p>Ionian Securities, subsidiary of state Ionian Bank </p>
<p>National Securities, subsidiary of state National Bank  </p>
<p>Commercial Securities, subsidiary of state Commercial Bank  </p>
<p>Nikiforos Securities</p>
<p>Based on the circular obtained by Reuters, Malakis also ordered inspectors on Monday to audit:</p>
<p>Avax Securities</p>
<p>Komninos Securities</p>
<p>Sarris Securities</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
